      "writtenOn": "2026-07-03T16:49:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This part of code was merged with unreviewed comments: this logic is broken because we\u0027re breaking the batch and performing individual apply-objects one by one.\n\nWhat I believe we should do is what has been suggested in https://gerrit-review.googlesource.com/c/plugins/pull-replication/+/377697/38/src/main/java/com/googlesource/gerrit/plugins/replication/pull/ReplicationQueue.java\n\n1. For all the `/meta` fetch all the history\n2. Create a new batch with the new `/meta` with the full history\n3. Re-try the batch\n\nIn this fix, you just retry the `/meta` and ignore the others.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 539,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 546,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "226a3c8d93fc350a493eca763768a106183cb494",
